-- Stock Sizer help page. Loaded on demand by OnLuaButton_InquiryHelp in Stock_Sizer.lua, the same way
-- Hold Down Helper loads its Help page, and shown in an HTML_Dialog. ButtonOK is the dialog's Close button.
]] -- =====================================================]]
function StockSizerHelpHtml()
    return [==[<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><title>Stock Sizer Help</title>
<style>
html { overflow: hidden; }
body { font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; background-color: #FFFFFF; color: #000000; margin: 0; overflow: hidden; }
.layout { overflow: auto; height: 540px; padding: 4px 14px 4px 10px; }
h1 { font-size: 20px; margin: 10px 0 4px 0; }
h2 { font-size: 16px; margin: 16px 0 4px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #999999; }
p, li { line-height: 1.35; }
table { border-collapse: collapse; margin: 4px 0; }
th, td { border: 1px solid #BBBBBB; padding: 3px 6px; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
th { background-color: #EEEEEE; }
.warn { background-color: #FFF4CE; border: 1px solid #D9A400; padding: 6px 8px; margin: 8px 0; }
.danger { background-color: #FDE2E1; border: 1px solid #C0392B; padding: 6px 8px; margin: 8px 0; }
.foot { text-align: center; padding: 8px; border-top: 1px solid #999999; }
.FormButton { font-weight: bold; font-size: 12px; }
</style></head>
<body>
<div class="layout">

<h1>Stock Sizer</h1>
<p>Stock Sizer finds the size of stock that a job needs, then it can change the sheet to that size. Thus you can
draw a job on a full 48 x 48 sheet and learn the stock size afterward. You do not have to change the sheet size
for each new job.</p>

<h2>Procedure</h2>
<ol>
<li>Draw the job on the <b>active sheet</b>.</li>
<li>Run Stock Sizer.</li>
<li>Set the values and push <b>Size Stock</b>.</li>
<li>If <b>Report only</b> is on, a message shows the sizes. The gadget does not change the sheet.</li>
<li>If <b>Report only</b> is off, a dialog shows the current size, the proposed size and the margin. Push
<b>Resize Sheet</b> to change the sheet. Push <b>Cancel</b> to keep the sheet as it is.</li>
</ol>
<div class="danger"><b>WARNING:</b> VCarve cannot undo a sheet size change. Save the job before you resize the
sheet.</div>

<h2>How the gadget finds the size</h2>
<ul>
<li>The gadget finds the bounding box of all visible vectors on the active sheet. The bounding box is the smallest
rectangle that holds all of the vectors. Grouped vectors are included.</li>
<li>Text and bitmaps have no vector outline. The gadget uses the bounding box of each one. The message tells you
when this happens.</li>
<li>The margin is the tool diameter plus the extra allowance. An outside profile puts the edge of the cutter a
full tool diameter outside the vector. The margin keeps the cutter on the stock.</li>
<li>The sheet keeps its <b>lower-left corner</b>. The new width and length go from this corner to the far edges
of the vectors, plus the margin. The gadget <b>does not move the vectors</b>.</li>
<li>If you select a value for <b>Round up to</b>, the width and the length each go up to the next multiple of
that value.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Settings</h2>
<p>All values are in the job units. The gadget keeps the values and the size of the dialog for the next run. It
keeps one set of values for inch jobs and a different set for metric jobs.</p>
<div class="warn"><b>CAUTION:</b> Type each value, then push the Tab key. VCarve does not keep a value that you
paste.</div>
<table>
<tr><th>Setting</th><th>Inch default</th><th>Metric default</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td>Largest tool diameter</td><td>0.25</td><td>6.0</td><td>The diameter of the largest cutter that cuts outside a
vector.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Extra allowance</td><td>0.125</td><td>3.0</td><td>An additional distance beyond the cutter, on each
side.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Round up to</td><td>None</td><td>None</td><td>None, 1/8, 1/4, 1/2 or 1 inch for an inch job. None, 1, 5,
10, 25 or 50 mm for a metric job. The width and the length go up to the next multiple of this value.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Report only</td><td>On</td><td>On</td><td>When it is on, the gadget shows the sizes and does not change the
sheet.</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>The messages</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Report:</b> The report shows the size of the vectors, the margin, the current sheet size and the stock that
the job needs where the vectors are now. If the stock is smaller when the vectors are at the lower-left corner,
the report also shows that size.</li>
<li><b>Confirmation:</b> This dialog shows the current size, the proposed size and the margin. It also shows any
warning.</li>
<li><b>Result:</b> After the resize, a message shows the new size.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Limits</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Vectors near the lower-left corner.</b> The gadget does not move the vectors. If the vectors are closer
than the margin to the left edge or to the bottom edge, the gadget shows a warning. Move the vectors away from the
corner before you resize the sheet.</li>
<li><b>Vectors away from the lower-left corner.</b> Space between the corner and the vectors stays in the sheet.
The report shows the smaller size of stock that you need if you move the vectors to the corner.</li>
<li><b>Hidden layers.</b> The gadget does not count hidden layers. Show all layers that the job cuts.</li>
<li><b>Active sheet only.</b> The gadget examines and changes only the active sheet.</li>
<li><b>Thickness.</b> The material thickness does not change.</li>
<li><b>Toolpaths.</b> The gadget does not change toolpaths. Calculate the toolpaths again after you resize the
sheet.</li>
</ul>

<h2>About</h2>
<p>Stock Sizer is an original gadget from the vectric-gadgets repository:<br>
<a href="https://github.com/tippmar/vectric-gadgets">https://github.com/tippmar/vectric-gadgets</a><br>
Questions and discussion: <a href="https://forum.vectric.com">Vectric User Forum</a></p>
<p><b>Disclaimer</b><br>
The Stock Sizer gadget is a plugin for Vectric software, VCarve Pro and Aspire.
Gadgets are an entirely optional add-in to Vectric's core software products.
They are provided 'as-is', without any express or implied warranty, and you make use of them entirely at your own
risk. In no event will the author(s) or Vectric Ltd. be held liable for any damages arising from their use.</p>
<p>Permission is granted to anyone to use this software for any purpose, including commercial applications, and to
alter it and redistribute it freely, subject to the following restrictions:</p>
<ol>
<li>The origin of this software must not be misrepresented; you must not claim that you wrote the original
software. If you use this software in a product, an acknowledgement in the product documentation would be
appreciated but is not required.</li>
<li>Altered source versions must be plainly marked as such, and must not be misrepresented as being the original
software.</li>
<li>This notice may not be removed or altered from any source distribution.</li>
</ol>

</div>
<div class="foot">
<input id="ButtonOK" class="FormButton" name="ButtonOK" type="button" value="Close">
</div>
</body></html>]==]
end
-- =============== End of File =========================]]
